        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-03-23T13:20:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Basically we've gotten some heavy implication that the Tactics timeline isn't merely awful, but actually actively dying, if we take the whole \"Prime War is the end of the Tactics universe\" part literally.</p><p>And also implications that said actual dying has something to do with the OblivAeon shards, the Mist Storm, the Void leaking into everything thanks to the Nexus being destroyed and not reforming, and whatever the Prime Wardens end up fighting against or doing in said Prime War.</p><p>I feel like this merits some speculation on how exactly these things all end up fitting together.</p><p>Like part of me wonders deeply if the universe ends up dying not because of what the Prime Wardens are fighting but because of what they themselves do (or not do) while fighting whatever it is.</p><p>Also, if the Tactics universe goes down and takes \"our\" Haka with it, aside from that you know really sucking, what implications does that have for Arataki?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:04.969Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
