        "raw": "One important thing we don't really know is how OblivAeon is defeated. The end of a timeline seems likely to involve OblivAeon or OblivAeon fallout somehow. So is OblivAeon dead? Incapacitated? Exiled? Can the shards \"re-form,\" or do they maintain some of OblivAeon's will and purpose? If Citizen Dawn activates too much shard power, does she awaken something?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnother angle on this is the Scions. We don't know what happens to them after OblivAeon's defeat. Is it possible Progeny is stomping around, grabbing OblivAeon shards and gaining some reality-collapsing powers?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI am also a little taken by the idea that - since the Prime Wardens prominently battled Progeny, oh, about...ten years before the OblivAeon event, and that happens to be the maturation time for a Maerynian, what if Tempest's offspring had some Progeny in them and then reacts poorly to the shards? What a tale that would be.",
