      {
        "id": 215598,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-03-23T21:56:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Personally I think the confluence of the Void leakage and the OblivAeon shards has something to do with it.</p><p>In the RPG universe, the Nexus eventually properly formed AND the OblivAeon shards seem to be much less numerous.</p><p>But in the Tactics universe, something kept the Nexus from reforming and the OblivAeon shards seem to have proliferated more.</p><p>I also feel like the fact that Akash'Bhuta absorbed the OblivAeon shards in the Tactics universe and more or less went bonkers might be relevant. Especially with also what Anthony's been doing with his own power and instruments. I mean \"don't mix Void magic and anything else\" is a pretty strong warning and now we have the two major Void-related entities on the planet doing precisely that.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
